3.1 Time series forecasting
The general goal behind forecasting is to predict the value of the
upcoming observations of oxygen concentration in a given cage,
ctC +1, …, ctC +h, given the historical data, where h denotes the
forecasting horizon.
We formalize the problem of time series forecasting based on an
auto-regressive strategy. Accordingly, observations of a time series
are modeled based on their recent lags. More precisely, the value of
ci is modeled based on the most recent q timesteps: Xi =
