3.2 Global forecasting models
Traditionally, forecasting models are trained using the historical
data of the time series of interest, often referred to as local models
(Januschowski et al., 2020 ). In our case, we need to forecast time
series from several cages that belong to multiple ﬁsh farms.
Leveraging the historical observations of all available time series
can be valuable to build a forecasting model. The dynamics of the
