For binary events, we can simply output the probability of that
event occurring. An instance of a binary event is exceedance, which,
as mentioned before, refers to when a time series exceeds a
predeﬁned threshold.
The probability of a hypoxia event hi denotes the probability that
the oxygen concentration ci falls below 7 mgL−1 in any given instant i.
In this type of problem, hi is usually modeled by resorting to a binary
target variable bi, which can be formalized as shown in Equation 1:
