multiple times. This idea is intuited in Figure 9 . This graphic
shows a sequence in which predictions are being produced over
time. Starting from time ti, four false alarms are triggered.
Performance evaluation should take the ﬁrst wrong prediction
into account as a false alarm. However, the subsequent false
alarms (as shown in Figure 9 ) are not meaningful since they', '{"doi": null, "filename": "662798dcee370224_03_forecasting-ocean-hypoxia-salmonid-fish-farms.pdf", "chunk_size": 1800, "topic_tags": ["dissolved_oxygen"], "species_tags": ["fish", "salmon"]}'::jsonb, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-04-15T11:59:59.639405+00:00');
